00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:11.900
Tamzin: I think early interventions, are
really key because having worked in lots

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.610
of different young people fields, I think
the sooner the young people get help with

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.439
whether it be antisocial behavior, whether
it be mental health issues, or whether

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:22.730
it be help with kind of school issues.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.870
Then the better outcomes they'll have.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.705
Fran: By getting in there early,
it's sort of, again, it demystifies

00:00:29.905 --> 00:00:31.365
mental health a little bit for them.

00:00:31.845 --> 00:00:36.205
It helps them find coping mechanisms
that can be quite lasting, I think.

00:00:36.205 --> 00:00:36.445
So.

00:00:36.445 --> 00:00:39.595
If someone learns some techniques
that help with their anxiety when

00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:42.970
they're 15, then there's a good
chance that those techniques will

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.410
still help them when they're 21.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.370
Tamzin: I think the earlier the better,
because we have a lot of young people

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:52.380
coming through when they're 16 or 15,
and older, where they've not even kind

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.560
of been assessed for special educational
needs and they find that they're

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.200
frustrated because, obviously, parents
are frustrated or carers are frustrated,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.740
the people are  frustrated because
they don't know what's wrong with them.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.300
Fran: I think someone who's maybe has had
some form of mental health support when

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:12.370
they're 13, 14, they're more likely to ask
for it when they're 18, 19 if something

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.600
happens or then again, when they're 30, if
something happens that they need support

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.065
with, because I think, I think it can
be harder and harder to ask for help the

00:01:20.065 --> 00:01:22.675
longer you go without ever receiving help.

00:01:22.745 --> 00:01:26.505
Tamzin: Early diagnosis is key because
then obviously the outcomes are the

00:01:26.505 --> 00:01:28.155
more support at school for them.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:31.925
There'd be obviously more support
for the parents, more support for

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.795
them, obviously outside of school.

00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:37.305
Everything would be a lot easier
in terms of like early intervention

00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:40.105
for young people who are in
the criminal justice system.

00:01:40.515 --> 00:01:44.355
Fran: We're not going to solve everything
